            ['n' => 9, 'name' => 'Paris 9th', 'areas' => 'Nouvelle Athènes, Martyrs', 'profile' => 'Families', 'price' => '11,400', 'extra' => 'Lively Haussmann Paris, at softer prices than the neighbouring 8th for classic apartments. Nouvelle Athènes and Martyrs are the most sought-after districts; a wraparound balcony or an open view makes the difference at resale.', 'positives' => ['Family Haussmann homes at softer prices than the 8th', 'Martyrs and Nouvelle Athènes: food shops and village life', 'Eight metro lines, RER A and E'], 'audience' => 'An urban family or a busy couple who want Haussmann Paris at a contained price.', 'housing' => 'Family Haussmann apartments, bourgeois buildings, a few cobbled courtyards.', 'summary' => 'The 9th is lively Haussmann Paris, between the Opéra and Pigalle. Urban families find classic apartments here at more contained prices than in the neighbouring 8th or 2nd, with balconies or open views going first. Nouvelle Athènes, Martyrs, Saint-Georges and Grands Boulevards, between the Palais Garnier inaugurated in 1875 and the department stores of boulevard Haussmann.', 'metro' => ['2', '3', '7', '8', '9', '12', '13', '14'], 'rer' => ['A', 'E'], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Palais Garnier', 'Galeries Lafayette', 'Printemps Haussmann', 'Musée de la Vie romantique', 'Grévin Museum', 'Folies Bergère', 'Gustave-Moreau Museum'], 'dining' => ['Rue des Martyrs', 'Rue Cadet', 'Bouillon Chartier', 'Marché Anvers', 'Rue Notre-Dame-de-Lorette'], 'parks' => ['Square Montholon', 'Square d\'Anvers - Jean-Claude-Carrière', 'Square Berlioz', 'Square Alex-Biscarre'], 'education' => ['Lycée Condorcet', 'Lycée Jules-Ferry', 'Lycée Jacques-Decour', 'Conservatoire national supérieur d\'art dramatique', 'Lycée Lamartine']],
            ['n' => 10, 'name' => 'Paris 10th', 'areas' => 'Canal Saint-Martin, Gare du Nord', 'profile' => 'Investors', 'price' => '10,200', 'extra' => 'A creative arrondissement still below central prices, driven by the canal and the two stations. Renovated buildings along the canal Saint-Martin are the most sought after; check the condition of the common areas in the faubourg, often the weak point.', 'positives' => ['Prices still below the centre, on the rise', 'Eurostar, Thalys, RER B, D and E: the gateway to the north', 'Canal and faubourg: the creative quarter of Paris'], 'audience' => 'An investor or a young buyer betting on appreciation.', 'housing' => 'Renovated period buildings, lofts, corner apartments on the canal.', 'summary' => 'The 10th is the arrondissement of the canal Saint-Martin and the two major stations, the most creative in eastern Paris. Prices stay below the centre and rise with the renovation of period buildings: lofts, corner apartments on the canal and small rental units attract investors and young buyers. Canal, Faubourg-Saint-Denis, Château-d\'Eau and Lariboisière, around the canal dug in 1825 and gare du Nord, Europe\'s busiest railway station.', 'metro' => ['2', '4', '5', '7', '8', '9', '11'], 'rer' => ['B', 'D', 'E'], 'stations' => ['Gare du Nord', 'Gare de l\'Est'], 'attractions' => ['Canal Saint-Martin', 'Porte Saint-Denis and porte Saint-Martin', 'Passage Brady', 'Point Éphémère', 'Saint-Louis hospital (historic courtyard)', 'Théâtre des Bouffes du Nord'], 'dining' => ['Rue du Faubourg-Saint-Denis', 'Passage Brady', 'Marché Saint-Quentin', 'Quai de Valmy', 'Rue Sainte-Marthe'], 'parks' => ['Villemin Garden', 'Canal Saint-Martin banks', 'Square Alban-Satragne', 'Square Juliette-Dodu'], 'education' => ['Lycée Colbert', 'Lycée Jules-Siegfried', 'Lycée Marie-Laurencin', 'Université Paris Cité (Villemin site)']],
            ['n' => 11, 'name' => 'Paris 11th', 'areas' => 'Oberkampf, Voltaire', 'profile' => 'Investors', 'price' => '10,600', 'extra' => 'The most liquid rental market in Paris: studios and one-bedrooms let without vacancy to young professionals. Oberkampf and Charonne for the buzz, Voltaire and Nation for families; former workshops on a courtyard are the rare finds.', 'positives' => ['The most liquid rental market in Paris', 'Prices below the Marais, five minutes on foot', 'Seven metro lines and RER A'], 'audience' => 'A buy-to-let investor or a first-time buyer.', 'housing' => 'Studios and one-bedroom flats, faubourg buildings, converted workshops.', 'summary' => 'The 11th is the most populated arrondissement in Paris, home to Bastille, Oberkampf and Charonne. Studios and one-bedrooms in faubourg buildings let without vacancy to young professionals, making it the first choice of investors, at prices well below the nearby Marais. Oberkampf, Voltaire, Roquette and Nation, between place de la Bastille and the Atelier des Lumières opened in 2018 in a former foundry.', 'metro' => ['1', '2', '3', '5', '8', '9', '11'], 'rer' => ['A'], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Place de la Bastille', 'Atelier des Lumières', 'Cirque d\'Hiver', 'Rue Oberkampf', 'Édith Piaf Museum', 'Bataclan'], 'dining' => ['Rue Oberkampf', 'Rue de Charonne', 'Marché Popincourt', 'Septime', 'Clamato', 'Rue Jean-Pierre-Timbaud'], 'parks' => ['Square Maurice-Gardette', 'Truillot Garden', 'Square de la Roquette', 'Boulevard Richard-Lenoir promenade'], 'education' => ['ESCP Business School', 'Lycée Voltaire', 'Lycée Dorian', 'Lycée Paul-Poiret']],
            ['n' => 12, 'name' => 'Paris 12th', 'areas' => 'Bercy, Nation', 'profile' => 'Families', 'price' => '9,700', 'extra' => 'Space, greenery and balconies at some of the most accessible prices in Paris, for families. Aligre and the Coulée verte are the rising areas; 1970s residences offer the best square metres for the price.', 'positives' => ['Among the most accessible prices inside Paris', 'Bois de Vincennes, Bercy, Coulée verte: the greenest', 'Gare de Lyon, line 14, RER A and D'], 'audience' => 'A family seeking space and greenery without leaving Paris.', 'housing' => 'Family apartments, 1970s residences with balconies, rare townhouses.', 'summary' => 'The 12th is the large family arrondissement of the east, from the faubourg Saint-Antoine to the bois de Vincennes. Families buy space and balconies here at some of the most accessible prices in Paris, townhouses and apartments along the Coulée verte being the most contested. Aligre, Bercy, Daumesnil and Picpus, between the Coulée verte opened in 1993 on the former railway and Bercy Village in 2001.', 'metro' => ['1', '6', '8', '14'], 'rer' => ['A', 'D'], 'stations' => ['Gare de Lyon', 'Gare de Bercy'], 'attractions' => ['Opéra Bastille', 'Bercy Village', 'Accor Arena', 'Viaduc des Arts', 'Cinémathèque française', 'Palais de la Porte Dorée', 'Château de Vincennes (next door)'], 'dining' => ['Marché d\'Aligre', 'Le Train Bleu', 'Bercy Village', 'Rue du Faubourg-Saint-Antoine', 'Marché Daumesnil'], 'parks' => ['Bois de Vincennes', 'Parc de Bercy', 'Coulée verte René-Dumont', 'Parc floral', 'Lac Daumesnil'], 'education' => ['Université Sorbonne Nouvelle (Nation campus)', 'École Boulle', 'Lycée Paul-Valéry', 'Lycée Arago', 'Lycée Élisa-Lemonnier']],
            ['n' => 13, 'name' => 'Paris 13th', 'areas' => 'Butte-aux-Cailles, Bibliothèque', 'profile' => 'Investors', 'price' => '9,200', 'extra' => 'New builds on the banks of the Seine and contained prices, to invest or settle as a family. Paris Rive Gauche for recent buildings and line 14, the Butte-aux-Cailles for the village houses that go within days.', 'positives' => ['New builds in Paris, on the banks of the Seine', 'Contained prices, universities and tech hub', 'Butte-aux-Cailles: much sought-after village houses'], 'audience' => 'An investor or a family drawn to new-build and contained prices.', 'housing' => 'New buildings, small houses on the Butte, renovated estates.', 'summary' => 'The 13th is the fastest-changing arrondissement, between the Bibliothèque nationale and the Butte-aux-Cailles. New builds along the Seine and contained prices attract investors and young families, while the small houses of the Butte sell within days. Gobelins, Butte-aux-Cailles, Olympiades and Paris Rive Gauche, around the BnF opened in 1996 and Station F, the world\'s largest start-up campus, inaugurated in 2017.', 'metro' => ['5', '6', '7', '10', '14'], 'rer' => ['C'], 'stations' => ['Gare d\'Austerlitz'], 'attractions' => ['Bibliothèque nationale de France', 'Butte-aux-Cailles', 'Gobelins Manufactory', 'Asian quarter (avenue de Choisy)', 'Boulevard Vincent-Auriol street art', 'Station F', 'Cité de la mode et du design'], 'dining' => ['Asian quarter', 'Butte-aux-Cailles', 'Marché Auguste-Blanqui', 'Rue de Tolbiac', 'Quai d\'Austerlitz (barges)'], 'parks' => ['Parc de Choisy', 'Parc Kellermann', 'Square René-Le Gall', 'Grands-Moulins - Abbé-Pierre Garden', 'Seine riverbanks'], 'education' => ['Université Paris Cité (Grands Moulins)', 'Université Paris 1 (Tolbiac)', 'Inalco', 'École nationale supérieure d\'architecture Paris-Val de Seine', 'Lycée Claude-Monet', 'Lycée Rodin']],
            ['n' => 14, 'name' => 'Paris 14th', 'areas' => 'Montparnasse, Alésia', 'profile' => 'Families', 'price' => '10,300', 'extra' => 'The residential calm of the southern Left Bank, at a clear discount to the neighbouring 6th. The villas and artists\' colonies of Pernety and Alésia are the most contested homes; Montparnasse offers the best connections.', 'positives' => ['Clear discount to the neighbouring 6th', 'Villas and artists\' colonies: houses inside Paris', 'Lines 4, 6, 12, 13 and RER B: the whole south'], 'audience' => 'A family or a couple who favour the calm of the Left Bank.', 'housing' => 'Bourgeois apartments, 1960s residences, villas and artists\' cités.', 'summary' => 'The 14th is the residential, family arrondissement of the southern Left Bank, between Montparnasse and parc Montsouris. Families buy bourgeois apartments and artists\' villas here at prices still reasonable for western Paris, the houses of Pernety and Alésia going first. Montparnasse, Daguerre, Alésia and Pernety, around the park opened in 1878 and the Cité internationale universitaire founded in 1925.', 'metro' => ['4', '6', '12', '13'], 'rer' => ['B'], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Paris Catacombs', 'Fondation Cartier pour l\'art contemporain', 'Cité internationale universitaire', 'Paris Observatory', 'Fondation Henri Cartier-Bresson', 'Rue Daguerre', 'Villa Seurat'], 'dining' => ['Rue Daguerre', 'Marché Edgar-Quinet', 'La Coupole', 'Rue Didot', 'Rue de la Gaîté'], 'parks' => ['Parc Montsouris', 'Cité internationale universitaire park', 'Square du Serment-de-Koufra', 'ZAC Didot garden'], 'education' => ['Cité internationale universitaire de Paris', 'École spéciale d\'architecture', 'Lycée Paul-Bert', 'Lycée François-Villon', 'Lycée Raspail']],
            ['n' => 15, 'name' => 'Paris 15th', 'areas' => 'Vaugirard, Convention', 'profile' => 'Families', 'price' => '10,400', 'extra' => 'The largest family arrondissement in Paris, peaceful and well equipped, below the prices of the 7th. Commerce and Convention for neighbourhood life, the Seine front for views and balconies; schools make the value of a street.', 'positives' => ['Family-friendly, quiet, priced below the 7th', 'Plenty of balconies and residences with space', 'Gare Montparnasse: Brittany and the South-West direct'], 'audience' => 'A family wanting a large apartment without leaving the Left Bank.', 'housing' => 'Large 1930s to 1970s apartments with balconies, high-end buildings, some Haussmann.', 'summary' => 'The 15th is the most populous arrondissement in Paris and the quietest of the large family districts. Families buy Haussmann, 1930s or 1970s apartments with balconies here at prices below the neighbouring 7th, with homes near parc André-Citroën and Commerce the most in demand. Vaugirard, Convention, Commerce and Front de Seine, around the park opened in 1992 on the former Citroën plant and the 1973 Montparnasse Tower.', 'metro' => ['6', '8', '10', '12', '13'], 'rer' => ['C'], 'stations' => ['Gare Montparnasse'], 'attractions' => ['Montparnasse Tower', 'Bourdelle Museum', 'Beaugrenelle', 'Porte de Versailles exhibition centre', 'La Ruche (artists\' colony)', 'Institut Pasteur (museum)', 'Statue of Liberty (île aux Cygnes)'], 'dining' => ['Rue du Commerce', 'Marché de Grenelle', 'Rue de la Convention', 'Rue Lecourbe', 'Marché Saint-Charles'], 'parks' => ['Parc André-Citroën', 'Parc Georges-Brassens', 'Île aux Cygnes', 'Square Saint-Lambert', 'Parc Suzanne-Lenglen'], 'education' => ['Institut Pasteur', 'Isep', 'Necker medical school (Université Paris Cité)', 'Lycée Buffon', 'Lycée Camille-Sée', 'Lycée Roger-Verlomme']],
            ['n' => 16, 'name' => 'Paris 16th', 'areas' => 'Passy, Auteuil, Trocadéro', 'profile' => 'Families', 'price' => '11,000', 'extra' => 'The bourgeois arrondissement par excellence: schools, calm, greenery and top-end buildings. Trocadéro and Passy for prestige, Auteuil for gated villas and softer prices; a parking space and a concierge count at resale.', 'positives' => ['Janson-de-Sailly, Molière, Dauphine: the families\' choice', 'Gated villas and private mansions', 'Bois de Boulogne and Ranelagh: the greenest west'], 'audience' => 'An international family or a buyer seeking surface and serenity.', 'housing' => 'Large Haussmann and Art Deco apartments, private mansions, private villas.', 'summary' => 'The 16th is the bourgeois arrondissement par excellence, backing onto the bois de Boulogne. Families buy here for the lycées, the calm and the greenery: top-end buildings, private mansions and gated villas, with higher prices around Trocadéro and Passy, softer towards Auteuil and porte de Saint-Cloud. Passy, Auteuil, Trocadéro and la Muette, between the Fondation Louis Vuitton opened in 2014 and the 1928 Roland-Garros stadium.', 'metro' => ['2', '6', '9', '10'], 'rer' => ['C'], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Trocadéro', 'Fondation Louis Vuitton', 'Marmottan Monet Museum', 'Palais de Tokyo', 'Guimet Museum', 'Roland-Garros', 'Parc des Princes', 'Maison de la Radio et de la Musique'], 'dining' => ['Rue de Passy', 'Marché du Président-Wilson', 'Rue d\'Auteuil', 'Le Pré Catelan', 'Marché de Passy'], 'parks' => ['Bois de Boulogne', 'Ranelagh Garden', 'Trocadéro gardens', 'Jardin d\'Acclimatation', 'Auteuil greenhouses'], 'education' => ['Université Paris Dauphine - PSL', 'Lycée Janson-de-Sailly', 'Lycée Molière', 'Lycée Jean-Baptiste-Say', 'Lycée Saint-Jean-de-Passy', 'Lycée La Fontaine', 'Lycée Claude-Bernard']],
            ['n' => 17, 'name' => 'Paris 17th', 'areas' => 'Batignolles, Ternes', 'profile' => 'Families', 'price' => '11,200', 'extra' => 'The fastest-rising arrondissement in the west, between bourgeois Haussmann homes and the eco-district. Batignolles attracts young families, Ternes and Monceau remain the safe bets; line 14 and RER E have changed the game at Porte Maillot.', 'positives' => ['Prices below the 8th and 16th for the same quality', 'Batignolles: village, families and new builds', 'Line 14 and RER E: Porte Maillot connected since 2024'], 'audience' => 'A family looking for a quiet, bourgeois district.', 'housing' => 'Haussmann apartments, recent Batignolles buildings, artists\' cités.', 'summary' => 'The 17th is the fastest-rising arrondissement in the west, from Ternes to Batignolles. Young families buy Haussmann homes here at prices below the neighbouring 8th and 16th, while the new builds of Clichy-Batignolles attract investors and first-time buyers. Ternes, Monceau, Batignolles and Épinettes, around parc Martin-Luther-King completed in 2020, the Paris courthouse opened in 2018 and porte Maillot served by RER E since 2024.', 'metro' => ['1', '2', '3', '13', '14'], 'rer' => ['C', 'E'], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Palais des Congrès', 'Paris courthouse', 'Square des Batignolles', 'Marché Poncelet', 'Sainte-Marie-des-Batignolles church', 'Arc de Triomphe (next door)'], 'dining' => ['Rue Poncelet', 'Rue de Lévis', 'Les Batignolles', 'Batignolles organic market', 'Rue des Dames'], 'parks' => ['Parc Clichy-Batignolles - Martin-Luther-King', 'Square des Batignolles', 'Parc Monceau (next door)', 'Square des Épinettes'], 'education' => ['Lycée Carnot', 'Lycée Honoré-de-Balzac', 'Lycée Jean-Drouant (hospitality)', 'Lycée Sainte-Ursule', 'Collège Stéphane-Mallarmé']],
            ['n' => 18, 'name' => 'Paris 18th', 'areas' => 'Montmartre, Abbesses', 'profile' => 'Pied-à-terre', 'price' => '9,500', 'extra' => 'The hill, its views and its village atmosphere, with prices that change from one street to the next. Abbesses and Lamarck for studios and views, Jules-Joffrin for families; check the exposure and the staircase, they make everything here.', 'positives' => ['Views over all of Paris from the hill', 'Two markets in one: Abbesses and districts on the rise', 'Artists\' studios and unique staircase houses'], 'audience' => 'A charming pied-à-terre, or an investor won over by the atmosphere.', 'housing' => 'Period apartments with views, artists\' studios, small houses on the Butte.', 'summary' => 'The 18th is the arrondissement of Montmartre, the most visited village in Paris, and of working-class districts in full transformation. Prices vary more than anywhere else from one street to the next: studios and apartments with a view of the hill sell at upscale prices, while the Goutte-d\'Or and la Chapelle remain among the cheapest in Paris. Abbesses, Lamarck, Jules-Joffrin and Clignancourt, around the Sacré-Cœur consecrated in 1919 and the Clos Montmartre vines planted in 1933.', 'metro' => ['2', '4', '12', '13'], 'rer' => [], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Sacré-Cœur', 'Place du Tertre', 'Moulin Rouge', 'Montmartre Museum', 'Halle Saint-Pierre', 'Clos Montmartre vineyard', 'Saint-Ouen flea market (next door)'], 'dining' => ['Rue des Abbesses', 'Rue Lepic', 'Marché Dejean', 'Rue Ordener', 'Rue du Poteau'], 'parks' => ['Square Louise-Michel', 'Renoir gardens (Montmartre Museum)', 'Square Léon', 'Jardins d\'Éole', 'Parc Chapelle-Charbon'], 'education' => ['Lycée Rabelais', 'Lycée Auguste-Renoir (applied arts)', 'Campus Condorcet (porte de la Chapelle)', 'Lycée Camille-Jenatzy']],
            ['n' => 19, 'name' => 'Paris 19th', 'areas' => 'Buttes-Chaumont, Villette', 'profile' => 'Investors', 'price' => '8,600', 'extra' => 'Among the lowest entry prices in Paris, with two large parks and a unique cultural offer. Buttes-Chaumont and bassin de la Villette are the sought-after areas; an apartment overlooking the park always resells well.', 'positives' => ['Among the lowest prices in Paris', 'Buttes-Chaumont and Villette: the largest parks in the east', 'Philharmonie, Cité des sciences, Centquatre: culture on foot'], 'audience' => 'An investor or a first-time buyer wanting to get into Paris.', 'housing' => '1970s and 1980s residences, new buildings, Mouzaïa houses.', 'summary' => 'The 19th is the greenest and most cultural arrondissement of the north-east, from the Buttes-Chaumont to la Villette. Prices are among the lowest in Paris, attracting families, young professionals and artists, with apartments overlooking the park or the bassin de la Villette going first. Buttes-Chaumont, Villette, Jourdain and Rosa Parks, around the park inaugurated in 1867 and the Philharmonie de Paris opened in 2015.', 'metro' => ['2', '5', '7', '7bis', '11'], 'rer' => ['E'], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Parc de la Villette', 'Cité des sciences et de l\'industrie', 'Philharmonie de Paris', 'Bassin de la Villette', 'Le Centquatre', 'Cité de la musique', 'Butte Bergeyre'], 'dining' => ['Quai de la Loire', 'Rue de Meaux', 'Marché de Joinville', 'Upper rue de Belleville', 'Place des Fêtes'], 'parks' => ['Parc des Buttes-Chaumont', 'Parc de la Villette', 'Bassin de la Villette', 'Parc de la Butte-du-Chapeau-Rouge', 'Canal de l\'Ourcq'], 'education' => ['Conservatoire national supérieur de musique et de danse', 'École nationale supérieure d\'architecture Paris-La Villette', 'Cours Florent', 'Lycée Henri-Bergson', 'Lycée Diderot']],
            ['n' => 20, 'name' => 'Paris 20th', 'areas' => 'Ménilmontant, Père-Lachaise', 'profile' => 'Investors', 'price' => '9,000', 'extra' => 'Village, studios and real upside potential, for a first purchase or an investment. Ménilmontant and Gambetta are the rising districts, la Campagne à Paris the rare gem; favour buildings with a recent façade renovation.', 'positives' => ['Among the most accessible prices in the capital', 'Campagne à Paris houses and studios: rare properties', 'Belleville and Ménilmontant: the Paris of artists'], 'audience' => 'An investor or a buyer looking for authenticity.', 'housing' => 'Faubourg buildings, converted workshops, townhouses with small gardens.', 'summary' => 'The 20th is the working-class, cosmopolitan Paris of artists, from Belleville to Charonne, with Père-Lachaise at its heart. First-time buyers and investors find some of the most accessible prices in the capital here, the houses of la Campagne à Paris and the studios of Ménilmontant being the most contested. Belleville, Ménilmontant, Gambetta and Charonne, around the cemetery opened in 1804 and the parc de Belleville viewpoint, the highest point of eastern Paris.', 'metro' => ['1', '2', '3', '3bis', '9', '11'], 'rer' => ['A'], 'stations' => [], 'attractions' => ['Père-Lachaise cemetery', 'Parc de Belleville (viewpoint)', 'Belleville murals', 'La Bellevilloise', 'La Campagne à Paris', 'Pavillon Carré de Baudouin', 'Villa de l\'Ermitage'], 'dining' => ['Rue de Ménilmontant', 'Rue de Belleville', 'Marché de Belleville', 'Rue des Pyrénées', 'Place Gambetta'], 'parks' => ['Parc de Belleville', 'Père-Lachaise cemetery', 'Pierre-Emmanuel natural garden', 'Square Séverine', 'Square Sarah-Bernhardt'], 'education' => ['Lycée Hélène-Boucher', 'Lycée Maurice-Ravel', 'Lycée Charles-de-Gaulle', 'Lycée Martin-Nadaud', 'Collège Françoise-Dolto']],
