                'items' => [
                    ['question' => 'Can foreigners buy property in Paris?', 'answer' => 'Yes. There are no restrictions on foreign nationals purchasing residential property in France. Our advisors guide international buyers through every step, from financing to the signing at the notary.'],
                    ['question' => 'How long does it take to buy a property in Paris?', 'answer' => 'Allow three to four months between the accepted offer and the final deed: a ten-day cooling-off period after the preliminary agreement, then the mortgage approval and the notary checks. Without financing, a purchase can complete in two months.'],
                    ['question' => 'What additional costs should I expect when buying?', 'answer' => 'Notary fees represent about 7 to 8% of the price for an existing property and 2 to 3% for a new build. Agency fees, when payable by the buyer, are stated in each listing.'],
                    ['question' => 'Can you help me find off-market properties?', 'answer' => 'Yes. Part of the properties we offer are never published: they are presented discreetly to a restricted circle of qualified buyers. [Entrust us with your search](contact) to gain access.'],
                    ['question' => 'Do I need to be in France to purchase a property?', 'answer' => 'No. Viewings can be done remotely, and both the preliminary agreement and the final deed can be signed by power of attorney. We coordinate the notary, the financing and the management of the property after the purchase.'],
                    ['question' => 'Can a foreign buyer get a mortgage in France?', 'answer' => 'Yes, French banks lend to non-residents, usually up to 50 to 70% of the price with a higher deposit than for residents. We introduce you to brokers used to international files.'],
                    ['question' => 'What is the difference between a promesse and a compromis de vente?', 'answer' => 'A promesse binds the seller for a set period while the buyer pays a deposit of about 10%. A compromis binds both parties from signing. In Paris the promesse is the most common form.'],
                    ['question' => 'What is the cooling-off period?', 'answer' => 'After signing the preliminary agreement, a non-professional buyer has ten days to withdraw without reason or penalty. After that, the buyer is bound subject to the conditions precedent, such as obtaining the loan.'],
                    ['question' => 'How does a viewing with Estate in Paris work?', 'answer' => 'We shortlist the properties matching your criteria beforehand, then group the viewings on a single day if you travel from afar. An advisor accompanies every viewing and answers your questions about the neighbourhood and the building.'],
                    ['question' => 'Which documents should I check before buying in a co-owned building?', 'answer' => 'The minutes of the last three general meetings, the co-ownership rules, the maintenance log, the technical surveys and the amount of the service charges. We gather and review them with you before any offer.'],
                ],
            ],
            [
                'key' => 'selling',
                'title' => 'Selling property',
                'items' => [
                    ['question' => 'How long does it take to sell a luxury property in Paris?', 'answer' => 'Two to four months on average for a correctly priced property in the central arrondissements, from listing to the signing of the preliminary agreement. Exceptional or unusual properties can take longer, until the right buyer comes along.'],
                    ['question' => 'How does Estate in Paris value an apartment or a private mansion?', 'answer' => 'From recent actual transactions in the neighbourhood, the intrinsic qualities of the property (floor, view, quietness, features, condition) and the demand we observe among our buyers. [The valuation is free](estimate) and without obligation.'],
                    ['question' => 'Can I sell discreetly, without a public listing?', 'answer' => 'Yes. An off-market sale presents your property only to qualified buyers from our portfolio, with no advertising or sign. It is the option most of our sellers of exceptional properties choose.'],
                    ['question' => 'Which surveys are required to sell?', 'answer' => 'The technical survey file includes the energy performance certificate, asbestos, lead, electricity and gas depending on the age of the installations, termites in some areas, and the Carrez surface area in co-owned buildings. We organise them for you.'],
                    ['question' => 'Should I renovate before listing?', 'answer' => 'Rarely major works: buyers of luxury property often want to personalise. Light refreshing, decluttering and careful staging, however, speed up the sale and support the price.'],
                    ['question' => 'How do you present a property?', 'answer' => 'Professional photography and video, floor plans, a bilingual presentation file, home staging when needed, then targeted distribution to our buyers and, if you wish, on the French and international specialist portals.'],
                    ['question' => 'How is capital gains tax calculated?', 'answer' => 'A main residence is exempt. For other properties, the gain is taxed at 19% plus 17.2% social charges, with a progressive allowance leading to full exemption after 22 years for income tax and 30 years for social charges.'],
                    ['question' => 'Open mandate or exclusive mandate?', 'answer' => 'An exclusive mandate entrusts the sale to a single agency committed to a precise marketing plan; it avoids multiple listings, often read as a sign of difficulty. We recommend it for luxury properties.'],
                    ['question' => 'How do you qualify buyers?', 'answer' => 'Every buyer is qualified before any viewing: project, timeline, financing capacity. You only receive serious visitors, and we report to you after each viewing.'],
                    ['question' => 'Can I sell from abroad?', 'answer' => 'Yes. The preliminary agreement and the deed can be signed by an authenticated power of attorney drawn up at a notary or a consulate. We coordinate the surveys, the viewings and the exchanges with the notary while you are away.'],
                ],
            ],
            [
                'key' => 'investing',
                'title' => 'Investing in Paris',
                'items' => [
                    ['question' => 'Why invest in luxury real estate in Paris?', 'answer' => 'Paris remains one of the most sought-after markets in the world: limited supply in the central arrondissements, constant international demand and strong price resilience in the high-end segments make it a long-term asset.'],
                    ['question' => 'Which neighbourhoods should I favour for a long-term investment?', 'answer' => 'The Marais, Saint-Germain-des-Prés, the Golden Triangle, Plaine Monceau and western Paris concentrate the most liquid properties. Our advisors guide you according to your goal: rental yield, second home or inheritance planning.'],
                    ['question' => 'Do you help manage the property after the purchase?', 'answer' => 'Yes. We connect our clients with trusted partners for rental management, renovation works and concierge services, so that an investment from abroad stays simple to follow.'],
                    ['question' => 'What rental yield can I expect in Paris?', 'answer' => 'In the luxury segment, gross yields usually sit between 2 and 3.5%: the investment is justified first by capital security and long-term appreciation rather than immediate income.'],
                    ['question' => 'Can I let a property as a short-term furnished rental in Paris?', 'answer' => 'Tourist letting of a second home is strictly regulated in Paris and generally requires a change-of-use authorisation with compensation. Long-term furnished letting or the mobility lease remain simpler options.'],
                    ['question' => 'Should I buy in my own name or through a company?', 'answer' => 'Buying in your own name is the simplest; a French SCI makes joint ownership and inheritance easier. The right choice depends on your tax and family situation: we refer you to a notary or tax lawyer before the purchase.'],
                    ['question' => 'Which annual taxes does an owner pay in Paris?', 'answer' => 'Property tax, the residence tax on second homes and, above 1.3 million euros of net property wealth, the real estate wealth tax. We estimate these charges with you before any purchase.'],
                    ['question' => 'How is the Paris luxury market evolving?', 'answer' => 'After a moderate correction in 2023-2024, well-located exceptional properties have regained sustained demand, driven by international buyers. We publish our reading of the market every week in [the newsletter](newsletter).'],
                    ['question' => 'Can I buy a whole building or a private mansion?', 'answer' => 'Yes. These rare properties mostly change hands off-market. We assist families, family offices and investors with the search, the analysis and the negotiation.'],
                    ['question' => 'How long should I hold a property to make the purchase worthwhile?', 'answer' => 'Given the acquisition costs, allow at least five to seven years. For Paris luxury property, the investment horizon is rather ten years and beyond.'],
                ],
            ],
            [
                'key' => 'working',
                'title' => 'Working with Estate in Paris',
                'items' => [
                    ['question' => 'How can I get in touch with an advisor?', 'answer' => 'Through the [contact page form](contact), by phone during opening hours, or by email. An advisor calls you back within 30 minutes during opening hours.'],
                    ['question' => 'Which languages do you work in?', 'answer' => 'Our advisors work in French and English and coordinate everyone a transaction from abroad requires: notary, financing, power of attorney, property management.'],
                    ['question' => 'What are your fees?', 'answer' => 'Our fees are a percentage of the sale price and are set out in the mandate before any listing. They are stated in each listing, as required by regulation.'],
                    ['question' => 'Which types of property do you offer?', 'answer' => "High-end apartments, private mansions, whole buildings, artists' studios and unusual properties in Paris and its immediate surroundings, listed publicly or off-market."],
                    ['question' => 'How do you guarantee confidentiality?', 'answer' => 'No information about a property or a client is shared without written consent. Off-market properties are presented without an address and under a confidentiality agreement to qualified buyers only.'],
                    ['question' => 'Do you work with other agencies?', 'answer' => 'Yes, whenever it serves our clients: we collaborate with a network of fellow agents in France and abroad to widen a search or the distribution of a property.'],
                    ['question' => 'Do you offer a bespoke search service?', 'answer' => 'Yes. Under a search mandate, a dedicated advisor shortlists the properties, organises the viewings, negotiates and accompanies you through to signing, including for off-market properties.'],
                    ['question' => 'What are your opening hours?', 'answer' => 'Monday to Friday from 8am to 8pm and Saturday from 8am to noon. Outside these hours, leave us a message: we call you back as soon as we open.'],
                    ['question' => 'Where is your agency located?', 'answer' => 'In the heart of Saint-Germain-des-Prés, in the 6th arrondissement. The address and a map link are on [the contact page](contact); we welcome you by appointment.'],
                    ['question' => 'How can I receive your market insights?', 'answer' => 'By subscribing to [our weekly newsletter](newsletter): trends, prices, a selection of properties and off-market opportunities, every Monday in your inbox.'],
                ],
            ],
        ],
    ],
